From 48b29e851fe79db8572a8d8f1929165603ed7be6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 14:27:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] libgcc: microblaze: remove muldi3_hardproc

muldi3_hard.S defines muldi3_hardproc, a 64-bit multiply with the
hardware multiplier.  Nothing calls it: __muldi3 comes from libgcc2.c,
and no compiler output or other libgcc routine names muldi3_hardproc.

It is also wrong on little-endian.  It stores its operands and reloads
their 16-bit halves with lhui at offsets that assume big-endian, so on
microblazeel muldi3_hardproc (2, 1) returns 0.  Over a table of 59
64-bit values it gives 3344 wrong products out of 3481 on little-endian
and none on big-endian.  It also stores r5-r8 in the caller's argument
save area, and its name is in the user's namespace.

Remove it.

Assisted-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

libgcc/ChangeLog:

	* config/microblaze/muldi3_hard.S: Remove.
	* config/microblaze/t-microblaze (LIB2ADD): Remove muldi3_hard.S.
---
 libgcc/config/microblaze/muldi3_hard.S | 150 -------------------------
 libgcc/config/microblaze/t-microblaze  |   1 -
 2 files changed, 151 deletions(-)
 delete mode 100644 libgcc/config/microblaze/muldi3_hard.S

diff --git a/libgcc/config/microblaze/muldi3_hard.S b/libgcc/config/microblaze/muldi3_hard.S
deleted file mode 100644
index 316021d5d..000000000
--- a/libgcc/config/microblaze/muldi3_hard.S
+++ /dev/null
@@ -1,150 +0,0 @@
